    "notes": "Whole study read. Under the Chapter 2 boundary in the run record (rules 0.2, R8), items are kept only where the text concerns access to the labour market and the movement of foreign workers: the Open Balkan labour market memorandum and its effects (eased or facilitated mobility, simplified employment rules, opening the labour market upon EU accession) and the inflow of Serbian workers into North Macedonia. Left out: emigration statistics and patterns of Macedonian workers, wage differentials and outflow claims not linked in the text to labour market access or foreign workers, general labour-market statistics and occupational gaps, and the policy recommendations on active labour market, education and regional investment policy (general labour-market policy). Recommendation headings that introduce lists are not extracted (R9). ICT occupations are mentioned often; judged incidental to the technology theme because technology is not the subject of the claims. Speaker is Finance Think unless the text attributes the claim to another body. Revised under rules 0.2 and themes 1.1 on 29 October 2026: 36 items removed (R8, R9), one missed claim added as -0056, and eu_scale.applies_to added (null throughout). Revised under rules 0.3 and themes 1.2 on 29 October 2026: Open Balkan items about North Macedonian workers moving out removed (R13: -0019, -0022 to -0025), recommendation heading -0049 restored (R15) and TECH-DGOV restored on -0001 (R12)."
  },
